; A device-intrinsic library standing in for a DOWNSTREAM project's (a downstream
; LLM engine's intrinsics library was the reported case). It is deliberately written the
; way sarek/ppx_intrinsic/README.md tells a downstream project to write one,
; with public library names only, and it lives in a directory whose name has
; NO underscore and differs from the library name: the registered module path
; used to be guessed from the directory, and this layout is the one that broke
; (Bits.float_of_bits registered as ["Bits"] instead of
; ["Dstest_intrinsics"; "Bits"]).
;
; (kind ppx_rewriter) is what makes `(pps sarek.ppx dstest_intrinsics)` legal
; and gets this library's registrations linked into the kernel PPX driver.

(library
 (name dstest_intrinsics)
 (kind ppx_rewriter)
 (libraries spoc.registry sarek.ppx.lib)
 (preprocess
  (pps sarek.ppx.intrinsic)))
